<title>USA: Indiana/Ohio direct hogs steady - USDA.</title>
<headline>Indiana/Ohio direct hogs steady - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>SPRINGFIELD 1997-03-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>USDA said barrows and gilts were steady. Demand and movement were light with some buying interests out of the market. Top $50.50 per cwt.</p>
<p>US 1-2  230-260 lbs.  48.00-49.50, few 50.00-50.50</p>
<p>US 2-3  230-260 lbs.  43.00-48.00</p>
<p>		210-230 lbs.  38.50-43.00</p>
<p>Sows - steady in a light test. Top $48.50.</p>
<p>US 1-3  300-450 lbs. 39.00-42.00</p>
<p>		450-500 lbs. 42.00-43.50</p>
<p>		500-600 lbs. 45.00-46.50, few over 600 lbs.</p>
<p>46.00-48.50</p>
</text>
